  "commander": "Gisela, Blade of Goldnight",
  "description": "Tests CR 615.5 controller-chooses-order rule for replacement effect chains. Gisela is the commander (always available from command zone), so she's reliably on-battlefield from turn 6+. The deck packs MULTIPLE damage doublers (Furnace of Rath, Dictate of the Twin Gods, Fiery Emancipation, Curse of Bloodletting) — when ANY damage event happens with Gisela + a doubler both on the same side, the affected player chooses application order: double-then-halve vs halve-then-double can produce different rounded results. Also includes Heartless Hidetsugu for chained event interactions with Gisela. May 25 audit revision: removed Wound Reflection (mono-B, was silently excluded by Gisela's RW color identity check); added Curse of Bloodletting (mono-R doubler, replaces Wound Reflection); added Mother of Runes + Shielded by Faith to protect Gisela from Claude's spot-removal package (Path to Exile / Swords to Plowshares / Austere Command stripped Gisela 3 times in the May 25 game before any damage event with a doubler could fire). Removed Heroic Reinforcements + Soul Snare + Searing Spear to make room.",
